---It can be either the name of a [SoundPrototype](https://lua-api.factorio.com/latest/prototypes/SoundPrototype.html) defined in the data stage, or a path in the form `"type/name"`. The latter option can be sorted into four categories.
---
---The validity of a SoundPath can be verified at runtime using [LuaHelpers::is\_valid\_sound\_path](https://lua-api.factorio.com/latest/classes/LuaHelpers.html#is_valid_sound_path).
---
---The utility and ambient types each contain general use sound prototypes defined by the game itself.
---
---* `"utility"` - Uses [UtilitySounds](https://lua-api.factorio.com/latest/prototypes/UtilitySounds.html). Example: `"utility/wire_connect_pole"`
---* `"ambient"` - Uses [AmbientSound::sound](https://lua-api.factorio.com/latest/prototypes/AmbientSound.html#sound). Variable sounds cannot be used. Example: `"ambient/resource-deficiency"`
---
---The following types can be combined with any tile name as long as its prototype defines the corresponding sound.
---
---* `"tile-walking"` - Uses [TilePrototype::walking\_sound](https://lua-api.factorio.com/latest/prototypes/TilePrototype.html#walking_sound). Example: `"tile-walking/concrete"`
---* `"tile-mined"` - Uses [TilePrototype::mined\_sound](https://lua-api.factorio.com/latest/prototypes/TilePrototype.html#mined_sound)
---* `"tile-build-small"` - Uses [TilePrototype::build\_sound](https://lua-api.factorio.com/latest/prototypes/TilePrototype.html#build_sound). Example: `"tile-build-small/concrete"`
---* `"tile-build-medium"` - Uses [TilePrototype::build\_sound](https://lua-api.factorio.com/latest/prototypes/TilePrototype.html#build_sound)
---* `"tile-build-large"` - Uses [TilePrototype::build\_sound](https://lua-api.factorio.com/latest/prototypes/TilePrototype.html#build_sound)
---
---The following types can be combined with any entity name as long as its prototype defines the corresponding sound.
---
---* `"entity-build"` - Uses [EntityPrototype::build\_sound](https://lua-api.factorio.com/latest/prototypes/EntityPrototype.html#build_sound). Example: `"entity-build/wooden-chest"`
---* `"entity-mined"` - Uses [EntityPrototype::mined\_sound](https://lua-api.factorio.com/latest/prototypes/EntityPrototype.html#mined_sound)
---* `"entity-mining"` - Uses [EntityPrototype::mining\_sound](https://lua-api.factorio.com/latest/prototypes/EntityPrototype.html#mining_sound)
---* `"entity-rotated"` - Uses [EntityPrototype::rotated\_sound](https://lua-api.factorio.com/latest/prototypes/EntityPrototype.html#rotated_sound)
---* `"entity-open"` - Uses [EntityPrototype::open\_sound](https://lua-api.factorio.com/latest/prototypes/EntityPrototype.html#open_sound)
---* `"entity-close"` - Uses [EntityPrototype::close\_sound](https://lua-api.factorio.com/latest/prototypes/EntityPrototype.html#close_sound)
---
---The following types can be combined with any item name as long as its prototype defines the corresponding sound.
---
---* `"item-open"` - Uses [ItemPrototype::open\_sound](https://lua-api.factorio.com/latest/prototypes/ItemPrototype.html#open_sound). Example: `"item-open/modular-armor"`
---* `"item-close"` - Uses [ItemPrototype::close\_sound](https://lua-api.factorio.com/latest/prototypes/ItemPrototype.html#close_sound)
---* `"item-pick"` - Uses [ItemPrototype::pick\_sound](https://lua-api.factorio.com/latest/prototypes/ItemPrototype.html#pick_sound). Example: `"item-pick/transport-belt"`
---* `"item-drop"` - Uses [ItemPrototype::drop\_sound](https://lua-api.factorio.com/latest/prototypes/ItemPrototype.html#drop_sound)
---* `"item-move"` - Uses [ItemPrototype::inventory\_move\_sound](https://lua-api.factorio.com/latest/prototypes/ItemPrototype.html#inventory_move_sound)
---
---[View Documentation](https://lua-api.factorio.com/latest/concepts.html#SoundPath)
---@alias SoundPath string

---Defines which slider in the game's sound settings affects the volume of this sound. Furthermore, some sound types are mixed differently than others, e.g. zoom level effects are applied.
